00:12:15.845 --> 00:12:18.367
I like how we are very slowly escalating.

00:12:18.367 --> 00:12:19.867
- Is it duck time?

00:12:21.061 --> 00:12:22.311
Yes, oh my god.

00:12:24.651 --> 00:12:25.484
- [Samantha] For the entrée,

00:12:25.484 --> 00:12:26.795
we are starting with the Peking duck.

00:12:26.795 --> 00:12:28.439
It comes with three sides of vegetable:

00:12:28.439 --> 00:12:31.170
Asian pear, cucumber, and also scallion.

00:12:31.170 --> 00:12:32.847
- [Steven] My mouth glands,

00:12:32.847 --> 00:12:35.388
whatever saliva-producing
glands I have in my mouth,

00:12:35.388 --> 00:12:37.048
- [Andrew] That's a lot of glands.

00:12:37.048 --> 00:12:40.631
- [Steven] Have just
opened up the heavens.

00:12:41.455 --> 00:12:43.049
- [Andrew] Sounds like scissors on paper.

00:12:43.049 --> 00:12:44.978
- [Steven] I think my
next video should just be,

00:12:44.978 --> 00:12:47.064
I learn how to carve Peking duck.

00:12:47.064 --> 00:12:48.943
- You can't even do the wrap,

00:12:48.943 --> 00:12:50.453
you think you're gonna carve the duck?

00:12:50.453 --> 00:12:51.326
(laughs)

00:12:51.326 --> 00:12:52.374
- [Steven] Look how,

00:12:52.374 --> 00:12:53.374
oh my gosh, the fat.

00:12:53.374 --> 00:12:55.544
- [Andrew] That's the duck butter.

00:12:55.544 --> 00:12:57.140
That is the duck butter.

00:12:57.140 --> 00:12:58.473
- [Inga] Cheers.

00:13:03.123 --> 00:13:07.540
- Oh my gosh, it's so crispy
that every single like--

00:13:07.682 --> 00:13:09.765
- Is moist like a sponge.

00:13:09.765 --> 00:13:10.682
It's moist.

00:13:10.790 --> 00:13:12.350
I have to like swallow the juice

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:14.555
as I'm chewing the rest of the meat.

00:13:14.555 --> 00:13:15.720
Want to do pancake time?

00:13:15.720 --> 00:13:17.887
- [Steven] Aw, let's do it.

00:13:17.887 --> 00:13:20.387
Aw, let's build some pancakes.

00:13:22.746 --> 00:13:23.600
- Pretty good Steven.

00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:24.600
- Thank you.

00:13:26.815 --> 00:13:27.648
- Way to go.

00:13:27.648 --> 00:13:28.481
- Cheers.

00:13:32.592 --> 00:13:33.425
- Mmm.

00:13:33.425 --> 00:13:34.258
Aw, okay.

00:13:34.258 --> 00:13:36.341
See, this is how you eat.

00:13:37.355 --> 00:13:39.458
- For what you can get here in New York,

00:13:39.458 --> 00:13:41.503
this is probably the closest you can get.

00:13:41.503 --> 00:13:45.586
- To like the traditional,
in China, Peking Duck.

00:13:48.882 --> 00:13:49.715
- [Samantha] After the Peking duck,

00:13:49.715 --> 00:13:52.168
we're gonna start with
one of our classic dishes,

00:13:52.168 --> 00:13:54.335
which is Kung Pao Chicken.

00:13:56.167 --> 00:13:57.768
- Mmm, that has a very nice bite.

00:13:57.768 --> 00:13:59.305
- The spice is like, just there.

00:13:59.305 --> 00:14:00.624
- [Samantha] The next
dish is the orange beef.

00:14:00.624 --> 00:14:03.764
So, on the menu, it says
Marvelous Orange Beef,

00:14:03.764 --> 00:14:07.062
but in the Chinese character,
it just means Tang's chicken.

00:14:07.062 --> 00:14:08.903
Because there's no name for it.

00:14:08.903 --> 00:14:10.998
- [Andrew] It's like a beef nugget.

00:14:10.998 --> 00:14:13.291
And it's not orange overwhelmingly.

00:14:13.291 --> 00:14:15.641
- [Samantha] The next dish
we have is a Mapo Tofu,

00:14:15.641 --> 00:14:17.058
very tender tofu.

00:14:17.157 --> 00:14:18.862
- [Inga] The tofu is like, extra soft.

00:14:18.862 --> 00:14:20.241
- I like it 'cause it's
a little like, peppery,

00:14:20.241 --> 00:14:22.241
- We got to have the most delicious meat,

00:14:22.241 --> 00:14:24.550
before we amped up with the spice.

00:14:24.550 --> 00:14:26.907
And now the meal just gets
more and more exciting.

00:14:26.907 --> 00:14:27.740
- [Samantha] And of course,

00:14:27.740 --> 00:14:30.337
we have to have vegetables
when we have Chinese food.

00:14:30.337 --> 00:14:32.943
So we have a fried vegetable
dish, which is the string bean,

00:14:32.943 --> 00:14:34.212
and then you have the snow pea,

00:14:34.212 --> 00:14:36.870
which is poached in a chicken
broth that we make in-house.

00:14:36.870 --> 00:14:37.790
- [Steven] You know like, as a kid,

00:14:37.790 --> 00:14:39.990
I didn't understand why
people didn't like vegetables,

00:14:39.990 --> 00:14:41.760
because when you eat vegetables like this,

00:14:41.760 --> 00:14:43.330
there's no question that it's delicious.

00:14:43.330 --> 00:14:46.350
- I really like how we went
from light to heavy to light.

00:14:46.380 --> 00:14:48.310
- Peking duck, banquet feast mode.

00:14:48.340 --> 00:14:50.080
- Smart way to eat a delicious meat.

00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:52.460
- It's just like being able
to see all the foods laid out,

00:14:52.460 --> 00:14:54.770
and really really well balanced meal.

00:14:54.770 --> 00:14:56.920
They took a lot of time
to prepare each dish,

00:14:56.920 --> 00:14:58.370
and I really appreciate that.

00:14:58.750 --> 00:14:59.910
- New York City, baby.

00:14:59.910 --> 00:15:01.650
That's what I'm talking about.

00:15:01.650 --> 00:15:04.240
So Andrew, which Peking duck spot was

00:15:04.240 --> 00:15:05.740
